# {{name}} - wiki schema

{{about}}

This repository is a knowledge wiki kept by an LLM agent, after Andrej Karpathy's "LLM Wiki" pattern. The owner
brings sources and asks questions; the agent writes and maintains every page. Read this file before any work here.
It is the wiki's only rulebook: change it with the owner, never on your own.

## Layers

| Where | What | Written by |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `raw/` | sources exactly as they came: a web page as markdown, a memory file, a note from the owner, a pointer to a read-only repository; images and attachments in `raw/assets/` | the owner or the agent, once; never edited after |
| `wiki/<kind>/` | the pages | the agent only |
| `index.md` | the catalog: every page on one line, under the section of its kind | the agent, whenever a page is added or its point changes |
| `log.md` | what was done and when, append-only | the agent, one entry per operation |

Kinds, one folder each under `wiki/`:

- `sources` - one page per source in `raw/`: what it says, and the pages it changed
- `topics` - a concept, technique, trap or decision that holds beyond one project
- `projects` - one page per repository this wiki knows: where it lives, what it is, which pages concern it
- `answers` - an answer worth keeping: a comparison, an analysis, a question settled

A new kind is a new folder plus a `## <kind>` section in `index.md`, agreed with the owner and added to this list.

## Pages

- File name: lowercase ascii words joined by `-`, ending `.md` (`transaction-scope.md`). The name is the link.
- Link with `[[page-name]]` - no folder, no `.md`; `[[page-name|other words]]` to show other words. When two files
  share a name, put the kind in front: `[[topics/page-name]]`. A raw file is linked the same way, by its name.
- First line `# <Title>`, then one paragraph saying what the page holds, then the body.
- Every claim says where it comes from: a `## Sources` section at the end links the source pages or raw files it
  rests on.
- A claim a newer source contradicts is rewritten as it now stands - "was X, now Y (<date>, [[source]])" - never
  appended below the old one.
- Written in the language the owner asks in; names, commands, paths and API members stay as they are.
- No secrets: no key, token, password or private block. The wiki is plain text, pushed to its remote and read by
  every agent.

## A source from a read-only repository

A repository this wiki must not write into, or copy from, is a source by pointer: a file in `raw/` that starts with

    ---
    repo: <absolute path of the clone>
    sha: <the commit that was read, 7 to 40 hex>
    paths:
      - <a path inside it>
    ---

then what was read there and why. Pages link that raw file. When lint says the clone has moved past `sha`, read the
paths again, then add a new raw file with the new `sha`; the old one stays as it is.

## Operations

### ingest - a source into the wiki

1. Put the source in `raw/` as `<YYYY-MM-DD>-<short-name>.md` (a web page through a markdown reader, a note as the
   owner gave it); attachments in `raw/assets/`. Never edit it afterwards.
2. Read it and tell the owner its key points in a few lines; ask what to stress when that is unclear.
3. Write `wiki/sources/<short-name>.md`. Update or create every topic and project page it touches, linking both ways.
4. Add an `index.md` line for each new page under its kind; rewrite the summary of a page whose point changed.
5. Append to `log.md`: `## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest | <source title>`, then the pages touched on the lines below.
6. Run lint and fix every error before saying done.

### query - answer from the wiki, keep the good answers

1. Read `index.md` first, then the pages it points to; follow links; open `raw/` only when a page is not enough.
2. Answer with links to the pages used. Say what the wiki does not know rather than filling it in from memory.
3. An answer worth keeping becomes `wiki/answers/<name>.md` once the owner agrees: linked from the topic pages it
   concerns, an `index.md` line, and `## [YYYY-MM-DD] query | <the question>` in `log.md`.

### lint - keep it healthy

1. Free, always first: the lint command below. It checks links, page names, the index against `wiki/`, the log,
   orphan pages (a warning), secrets, and sources from read-only repositories.
2. Costs tokens, only when the owner asks and after saying how many pages and characters will be read:
   contradictions between pages, claims a newer source superseded, concepts mentioned without a page of their own,
   questions worth a new source.
3. Append `## [YYYY-MM-DD] lint | <what was checked>` to `log.md`.

### promote - from an agent's memory

An agent's memory belongs to one project and keeps what holds there. A fact that holds beyond that project comes
here, and only after the owner approved the list of memory files, the pages they become and what stays behind: copy
the memory file unchanged to `raw/memory/<project folder name>/`, ingest it, then leave in the memory file only its
project-specific part and one line pointing to the page. Log it as `promote`.

## Log entries

`## [YYYY-MM-DD] <op> | <title>`, op one of `init`, `ingest`, `query`, `promote`, `lint`; newest at the end, never
edited or reordered. Lines below an entry are free.

## Commands

- Lint, free, no model: `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "{{runner}}" lint -Wiki .` - the
  paper-kit copy that created this wiki; every project set up with paper-kit has one at
  `.claude/skills/wiki/scripts/wiki.ps1`.
- The last five log entries: `Select-String -Path log.md -Pattern '^## \[' | Select-Object -Last 5`
- Commit in this repository when the owner says so.
